t a complete banana hater i just  don't like them once they are  ripened but i keep my personal prejudice  aside because i know literally planet  earth loves bananas more than anything  and there's actually a lot of wastes  tied to bananas because once they reach  a certain point most people think that  they're inedible and want to toss them  in the trash so my first tasty video i  ever did was actually four different  ways to bake with ripe bananas literally  millions of bananas are tossed out every  day because people think that they're  too ripe and they don't like how they  look and funny enough the ripe bananas  are the ones you want to bake with so  if you have ripe bananas in your house  and you're like ugh i don't want to eat  that i feel you i understand put it in  the freezer bake with it later and you  can make some muffins  [Music]  this recipe was a journey  this is not a pour  so here's where trouble is right now  so this recipe took a lot of development  to nail down i mean  the amount of math and science figuring  out  volume of battery i needed for the whole  cake what i'm going to do is plop my  calculator  and figure out  within my two cups of chocolate amongst  four bowls and divided so i can properly  scale up  as well as how much stabilizer i needed  in order for the colors to not bleed  into each other  oh  oh to the top  the simplest way to approach this recipe  is i wanted to make one mother batter  for every color of the cheesecake and  then divide it into  four different bowls that way each bowl  got its own quantity of chocolate to  create a different tone of brown just  get in there  i feel like these are almost too close  in color  so maybe just a little bit more  so it can be very distinguished  part of the difficulty was just the  mechanics of  filming while cooking because when i  would put down a bowl to change camera  lenses  the batter itself would actually start  to set so the idea is to like pour them  all into the pan this is not  but you have to change the container  yeah so i'll put it into a  microwave-proof container  let's get started on fire  and 15 seconds  great yeah solutions by relay so each  batter has to remain kind of loose and  warm up until it's all done and then it  can go into the fridge and set so a tip  that i learned was  while making this cheesecake at any  point you have to stop or take a break  microwave the batter for 20 seconds or  so just to get it re-fluid before you  start pouring and wait until you have a  window time to pour all four colors  before you do it because if you pour  layer one and then take a break and then  try to pour layer two it's not gonna  push out and you're not gonna get a nice  beautiful even ring so it definitely  requires your full attention while  making fingers crossed for layer three  just like ready we're ready for you  layer three one layer three  we're living in like the twilight zone  right now you did it  this cheesecake is definitely one of the  more aspirational desserts i've made  it requires a lot of attention to detail  and patience so if you are a hobby baker  and you just want to like dedicate an  afternoon to making something like  really stunning and beautiful for your  friends or family for any occasion this  is definitely a fun recipe to like take  on as a challenge i really  have a genuine interest of knowing what  other flavors can be made with this  cheesecake so if you do make another  flavor please let us know pop in the  comments and  maybe i'll give it a try too  [Music]  this recipe is a total throwback to my  childhood back in elementary school we  had these magazines where you could  order christmas gifts for people and  they had this four flavored cheesecake  where it was four individual cheesecakes  cut up into quarters but all put  onto one piece of cardboard and i  figured i could probably try to make it  all in one pan  so what made this cheesecake a bit  tricky is that i wanted to divide up  four very 