vor was meant  to be caramel  but the consistency of that varied so  much between every product i use some  were super runny some were so thick i  could even fold them in and it was  really tough when i was testing this  recipe i thought the cheesecake was done  it was beautiful and then as we're  filming the beauty shots the caramel  completely fell apart it literally was  oozing out of the side of the pan  because there's way too much water in it  but our lovely friends in brazil have  created a great food product called  dolce de leche which has a very similar  taste to caramel but it's so smooth and  thick so once i figured to use that it  was smooth sailing from there  and all the flavors  were good to go  i wanted people to have the option of  having that like prized double flavor  slice of cheesecake where you cut a  quarter inch of what's on the left and  quarter on the right and you have like a  two for one special however i think all  the flavors go really well together but  i had to check so i tested double  forkfuls of all the flavors just to see  what went and the only one that really  didn't go too well was a lemon curd and  chocolate so in the final cheesecake i  put them on opposing ends and then  everything else was good from there the  most struggling part about developing  this recipe  was to make it simple i wanted to be  like very all levels friendly  it's easy to make things complicated  it's difficult to make them simple it's  my philosophy of recipe development this  video didn't take long at all to do  wow  took like a day  full play the cheesecake  cool

